SETTINGS RADIO toggles: clicking a DETAIL / SOUND-FX / MUSIC radio moves it + re-renders bit-identically.

The SKY checkbox toggle was bit-verified (patch 318), but the DETAIL / SOUND / MUSIC RADIO groups did
not respond to a click: the near-handler dispatch FUN_0000_6b27 dropped the handler-id register the
radio handlers need, and the DETAIL handler FUN_0000_6eb8 had a DGROUP base-loss (SIGSEGV) plus the
radio widgets' dirty flags were WORD-typed (the patch 318 store-width class).  Three asm-verified fixes
(vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin, DS=DGROUP=0x1c00); each radio now moves the lit indicator + updates the
status line byte-identically to the DOSBox reference (flows settings-detail-med / settings-sound-fx-med
/ settings-music-off).

1. FUN_0000_6b27 (asm 0x6b27: `call WORD PTR cs:[bx+0x6b2d]`).  The near-handler dispatch is entered
   with BX (the handler id, = param_1) STILL LIVE, and the radio handlers read it:
     6bcc: `sub bx,0x12; mov ax,bx; call 6eb8`   (DETAIL LOW/MED/HIGH -> value 0/2/4)
     6bd5: `sub bx,0x18; mov ax,bx; call 6ed4`   (MUSIC OFF/ON)
     6bde: `sub bx,0x1e; mov ax,bx; call 6ee2`   (SOUND-FX OFF/MED/HIGH)
   Ghidra emitted the dispatch ARG-LESS -> the radio handlers ran on a garbage bx.  Thread bx=param_1
   into the dispatched handler (the checkbox handlers 6b60/6bb1/6be7/6c02/6c1d take void and ignore the
   extra cdecl arg).  (The handler-id -> near-offset table read was already rebased by patch 318.)

2. FUN_0000_6eb8 (asm 0x6eb8: the DETAIL radio handler).  `a3 47 8b mov ds:0x8b47,ax` stores the value;
   `8b b7 3d 8b mov si,[bx-0x74c3]` (bx=ax, DS=DGROUP) reads the per-value status-string id from
   word[DGROUP:(param_1-0x74c3)] = 0x8b3d/0x8b3f/0x8b41 and 7018 sets the bottom status ("DETAIL SET TO
   LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH").  Ghidra dropped the DGROUP base -> `*(int*)(param_1-0x74c3)` = a raw host deref of
   the near-offset (fault 0xffff8b3f for MEDIUM).  Rebase to g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)(param_1-0x74c3).

3. The radio/checkbox widget DIRTY flags are BYTEs (asm `c6 06 .. 03  mov BYTE PTR ds:0xNN,0x3`) but
   were typed WORD (the patch 318 / 104 / 134 store-width class): the WORD `= 3` writes 0x0003, whose
   high byte clobbers the adjacent widget's renderer-index byte -> the dirty-walk 209e re-paints the
   WRONG renderer (a garbage sprite / no indicator move).  Retype to BYTE the eight radio dirty flags
   that are ONLY ever written `= 3`: 0x8bac/0x8baf/0x8bb2 (DETAIL, 6eb8), 0x8bb8/0x8bbb (MUSIC, 6ed4),
   0x8bc1/0x8bc4/0x8bc7 (SOUND-FX, 6ee2).

The state renderers (6cf4 DETAIL / 6d05 MUSIC / 6d16 SOUND-FX / 6ce5 SKY) and the sprite blit 6d54 were
already reconstructed (patch 132); this patch just makes the click reach them with the right state.

Result: byte-identical to the DOSBox reference on all three new flows (AE=0 native + wasm, native<->wasm
0-diff, deterministic 5x single md5).  Reached only by clicking a radio inside SETTINGS -> the prior
flows are behaviour-neutral (6b27's extra arg is ignored by every non-radio handler; 6eb8/the radio
dirty flags are touched only on a radio click; settings / settings-sky unchanged).

